WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:02.070
- [Announcer] This Great Big Story

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:04.670
was made possible by Shell.

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:06.470
Make the future.

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:08.150
- [Narrator] The wheel.

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:12.120
A perfect function
invented in the Stone Age.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:15.090
To this day, the wheel
provides the same function

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:17.480
as it did those thousands of years ago,

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:21.270
but one man is flipping
everything we knew about the wheel

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:22.450
on its head.

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:23.910
- My name is Michael Burtov.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:26.410
I'm not an engineer, but
I did what most engineers

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:27.243
wish they could.

00:00:31.156 --> 00:00:33.739
(gentle music)

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.100
When I was a little kid I
liked to take things apart

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.060
and see what they're made out of.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:40.790
I tried to make something new out of them.

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:43.470
And I still like doing it to this day.

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:46.060
In 2012, I was running an HR company,

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:47.560
and I turned on the movie, "Tron."

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:49.520
I was drinking a coffee, and I thought,

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:52.520
"Those are very cool
motorcycles in the movies."

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:53.620
They're called light cycles,

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:55.200
and they have these hollow wheels,

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.350
and I remember thinking, well,

00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:59.570
I'm not an engineer but
couldn't we do something useful

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:00.700
with that empty space?

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:02.870
I imagined you could
put things in the wheel

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:05.220
that lived outside of it
with an electric wheel.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:07.613
For example, the motor and the battery.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:13.750
A wheel that powers itself is
a much more universal wheel

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:17.003
than a wheel that needs
something else to power it.

00:01:17.003 --> 00:01:19.650
Make it super compact, super efficient,

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:21.400
and that's really what inspired me.

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:23.780
Pretty much everyone
said it was impossible.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:26.070
They said that if it could be done,

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:29.270
it would have been done
already by a real engineer.

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:31.270
So I ignored them, and I quit my job

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:34.290
and then I met Dakota Decker,
who ended up leaving SpaceX

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:36.090
to build the wheel together with me.

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:41.110
Dakota and I spent about two years

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:44.283
before we came to the version
that we put out for retail.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.970
It's a much more compact design.

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:51.080
Takes up the same space as a regular wheel

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:54.230
but has got everything in
it, the entire power train,

00:01:54.230 --> 00:01:57.030
the battery, the motor, the computer.

00:01:57.030 --> 00:01:59.320
This wheel is extremely
environmentally friendly.

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:02.083
It's electric powered, and
it's a very efficient use.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:06.310
We have made thousands of bicycles

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:09.570
into affordable, electric
vehicles all over the world.

00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:11.220
We see that we can
contribute to the future

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:13.910
of transportation with
the GeoOrbital wheel.

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:17.550
We see vehicles that
nobody has ever made before

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:19.710
being able to be made now.

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:21.930
Imagine a car, imagine the possibilities

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:24.470
when you take all the guts out of a car

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:26.130
'cause you just don't need them anymore.

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:28.800
The opportunity's really are endless.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:31.550
(dramatic music)

